## v0.8.0 – AWS Production Deployment & Local Dev Setup
**Date:** December 27, 2025 11:50 PM PST

### Changes Made:
- Deployed Astrotask to AWS using ECS Fargate (serverless containers)
- Set up Aurora Serverless v2 PostgreSQL database with auto-scaling
- Configured Application Load Balancer (ALB) with SSL via AWS ACM
- Created ECR repositories for backend and frontend container images
- Set up AWS Secrets Manager for secure environment variable storage
- Configured Namecheap DNS with CNAME records pointing to ALB
- Added `/health` endpoint to backend for ALB health checks
- Fixed CORS configuration to support `www.astrotask.io`
- Fixed ECS service subnet configuration (ALB availability zone mismatch)
- Changed encryption key storage from `sessionStorage` to `localStorage` for cross-tab support
- Fixed duplicate `/api/v1` in request-invite page API call
- Created shell functions for Docker build/tag/push/deploy workflow (`astro-backend-ship`, `astro-frontend-ship`)
- Set up simple local development environment with Docker Compose
- Created `.env.local` and `.env.example` templates with simple `localdev` credentials
- Removed obsolete `version` attribute from docker-compose.yml
- Completely rewrote README.md with comprehensive onboarding docs
- Created AWS deployment guide at `.claude/AWS_DEPLOYMENT.md`
- Created deployment session notes at `.claude/AWS_DEPLOYMENT_SESSION.md`

### Current Status:
- Production site live at https://www.astrotask.io
- Backend and frontend services running on ECS Fargate
- Database running on Aurora Serverless v2
- Invite system working - admin can create invites
- Local development working with Docker Compose
- All API endpoints functional

### Unresolved Issues:
- Apex domain `https://astrotask.io` times out (Namecheap can't handle HTTPS redirects for apex domains)
- Need to migrate DNS to AWS Route 53 to fix apex domain issue
- Should rotate compromised credentials from old .env files

